# The owner's secrets: keys for paid outside services. Placeholders only: never put a real key here.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.secrets` in the main checkout only (`cp .env.secrets.example .env.secrets`,
# then `chmod 600 .env.secrets`) and fill in your own values. Git ignores it, worktrees never get a
# copy, and agents may not read, edit or name it (the guard and the deny rules of
# .claude/settings.json). A command that needs a secret runs through `node harness/with-secrets.mjs
# -- <command>`, which reads this file of the main checkout and gives its values to that one
# process; a variable already set in the environment wins, which is how CI passes its repository
# secret. Settings that agents may see stay in `.env.example` (docs/permissions.md, "Environment
# files").
#
# Never export these in the shell that runs the phase loop or Claude Code: an ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in
# that environment would bill the agent sessions to it instead of the owner's subscription.

# Anthropic API key for the paid model evals (`apps/mcp-admin/evals/`, later the other eval
# suites). Use a separate development key with a low spend limit. CI's model evals use the
# repository secret of the same name instead (.github/workflows/model-evals.yml).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# The owner's admin API key: the same key the owner's MCP client sends to Admin MCP. Only the API's
# maintenance command `media upload` reads it, run as `node harness/with-secrets.mjs -- pnpm
# --silent --filter @sebela/api media upload <file>` (apps/api/AGENTS.md, Commands); a value
# already set in the shell wins. Create it with `api-keys create <name>` on the API it is meant
# for.
SEBELA_ADMIN_API_KEY=
